        {
          "id": 2612966258,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Hmm, that's surprising. I could believe it in the case of the `NL80211_RRF_` flags, but the `MPATH_FLAGS` enum values don't have the space there in the file from the 'wireless-next-2025-06-25' tag that you said you used:\n\nhttps://web.git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/wireless/wireless-next.git/plain/include/uapi/linux/nl80211.h?h=wireless-next-2025-06-25\n\nIf I download that file and run it with `tools/generate-nl80211-fields.py`, it does not insert the spaces there (though it does insert in the places where there were spaces in the file.)\n\nDid you perhaps open the file in an IDE or other editor that automatically applied style formatting to add extra spaces around the left shift operator? If so, I suspect that it would be easier to use the file exactly as it currently appears in the kernel git (even if the kernel maintainers may do a style update later for consistency.)",
